// =============================================================================
// LAKEFLOW CONNECT DIRECT CDC FROM ON-PREMISES SQL SERVER / ORACLE, THROUGH A
// PRIVATE NETWORK GATEWAY (AWS)
//
// JSONC for you to read; emit PLAIN JSON (strip the // lines) when you write
// architecture.md. Read reference/style-networking.md first. The Azure version of the
// same pattern is reference/lakeflow-cdc-png-azure.jsonc (read its header for what
// Direct CDC is); this one shows what changes on AWS.
//
// HOW IT WORKS ON DATABRICKS (use this to adapt the diagram to the user's setup):
//   • Direct CDC: ONE scheduled serverless Lakeflow Connect pipeline does the snapshot,
//     the CDC and the replication — no separate ingestion gateway. Being serverless, it
//     reaches the on-premises database through the Private Network Gateway (PNG).
//   • PNG on AWS (Private Preview, Enterprise tier): created inside the account's NCC;
//     Databricks puts a managed network interface in a dedicated /28 subnet of the
//     customer's VPC — exactly one subnet, so one AZ, in the preview. The customer
//     creates an IAM role in their AWS account that Databricks uses to create and
//     manage the PNG in that VPC.
//   • From the PNG subnet, traffic follows the VPC's routes: to the Transit Gateway,
//     then the Direct Connect gateway and Direct Connect / Site-to-Site VPN to the data
//     centre. The workspace VPC is attached to the same Transit Gateway; it is not on
//     the pipeline's path.
//   • Limits: Direct CDC is in Private Preview, SQL Server and Oracle only; during the
//     preview create the connection with SQL if the UI cannot. PNG is API only.
//
// WHAT IT DEMONSTRATES (layout):
//   • The top level runs in traffic order: Databricks account → AWS cloud (shared services
//     VPC → Transit Gateway → Direct Connect gateway) → the data centre. The hops on the red
//     path carry `track: "t1"`, so the path is one straight line.
//   • The private link (Direct Connect / S2S VPN) is the data-centre box subtitle (no Site-to-Site VPN
//     icon on AWS, and no clean label slot between two close borders).
//   • The IAM role is NOT on the data path: a dashed edge from the PNG says Databricks
//     uses it to create and manage the PNG. It sits under the VPC, inside the AWS cloud.
//   • The workspace VPC is one card, joined to the Transit Gateway by a dashed
//     "attachment" edge.
//
// ADAPT IT: name the user's databases. With no Transit Gateway (the PNG VPC itself has
// the Direct Connect / VPN), drop the Transit Gateway node and the attachment. For the Azure
// version see lakeflow-cdc-png-azure.jsonc; for no inbound connectivity at all, the
// on-prem agent (lakeflow-onprem-agent-azure.jsonc).
// =============================================================================
